===== 9. what this round does NOT establish =====
### * No device measurement at all: the device is in EDL, the fake root's /proc and /sys are synthetic,
###   and the *only* real numbers here are the raw zone values quoted from 2026-09-22.
### * The unit table is a table. It is derived from a measurement (558 = 55.8 C, 49 = 49 C), not from a
###   driver symbol, and it covers the six families this device has shown. A driver that reports deci
###   under a name in the milli row would be scaled wrong and the band would not catch it -- the raw
###   value and unit printed on the hottest line are the guard against that, and a new family is
###   supposed to be added to the table when it appears.
### * `pa_therm0/1` and `emmc_therm` were grouped with msm_therm/quiet_therm as plain degC in the
###   2026-09-22 units section, but msm_therm/quiet_therm are the two that were actually read and
###   quoted; if the pa_therm group turns out to be deci, the band will flag it loudly, which is the
###   behaviour scenario 2 pins.
### * The A/B ordering and the per-process union are asserted against a synthetic two-window run on
###   the host; neither has been exercised on the device.
